{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "game": "gi",
  "id": "sundjatta-s-first-foray",
  "name": "Sundjatta's First Foray",
  "sourceUrl": "https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Sundjatta%27s_First_Foray",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-07-18T08:35:01.727Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "vol-1",
      "label": "Vol. 1",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Oh, my brothers, my children, listen well,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Listen well to my name — Djeli Mamoudou of the Children of Echoes."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A singer am I of our tribe, a herald of epic tales."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "From Bilali, that first singer of sagas, does my line begin,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And Keitan Kouyate and Bintu Kouyate are my forebears."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Bilali it was who once followed a wandering sage to learn ancient verses,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And the Kouyates wove the ancient texts into carpets and felt tents."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "My mind comprehends the dragon-lords and barbarian kings of benighted ages,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "My tongue can engage the most verbose Monetoo in verse,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "My stories illuminate many truths, my words purify more falsehoods,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For stories cleanse untruths and become history, clear as a crystal mirror."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Such mirrors gleam with rainbow light from ancient days, but darkness too is dazzling,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Like a glimmer in the unfathomable eyes of the dead."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "History teaches the survivors, but stories are rooted in those who have passed..."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "As surely as gems of the future must spring from the veins of the past."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "So come, hear me sing, hear me tell of this hero,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Listen as I chant the soul-song of the children of the wild bull, the children of the rhinoceros."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I shall tell you of Magan Sundjatta, his deeds, and his fate,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I shall speak of Mali Djata's burdens and passion,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I shall sing praise of Sogolon Djata's illustrious reputation,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And of Nare Magan Djata's final battle against the great enemy..."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Oh, which hero has ever possessed so many titles?"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Neither the darkest magic nor the foulest wraith could hurt him!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "My brothers, my progeny, proud Children of Echoes,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Listen, and I shall tell you of a hundred thousand barbarian kings, now forgotten,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Harken as I tell you of their defeat at Sundjatta's hands,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And how, once conquered, they fought by his side,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Let me speak of how foes become friends, how savagery may yet birth goodwill..."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Let me tell of how the pitch-dark armies came forth like a mountain,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And how they dissolved before Sundjatta's might,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For this is a tale of great deeds once unrecorded, sacrifices misunderstood..."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-e66cf4024b0dabf4"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "volumeKey": "vol-2",
      "label": "Vol. 2",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It is as they say, that many who are wise are not of noble birth."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "So too had Sundjatta's lineage never been tainted by ancient royalty."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The old tales have faded like salt rivers in a darkened mine,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Leaving but shimmering crystals of truth for poets to reveal."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "So it is with Sundjatta, and many are the account of his birth."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Close friends may desire to embellish, and amongst enemies one shall find a lack of praise."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What were the names of his parents? Which tribe were they from?"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ask the pale light of three moons, and still you shall have no answer."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Story and song say Sundjatta was born blessed by the stars of dawn."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "No beauty his mother, no strongman his father,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But the celestial watcher-stars care not for mortal appearance,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For to weave the fate of heaven and earth alone is duty eternal, a task divine."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Mbande was chief of our tribe when Sundjatta was young,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Black-Jade Mbande, who was the mother of mines and gems,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "T'was she who chose him to be our tribe's hero."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And thus did his story begin, the hero great, the miner mighty."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When young Sundjatta began his career in the mines,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The mountain-carving hammers were larger than his whole body."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yet he wielded them as though he were the wind itself,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "So much so that heroes cried out, \"The mine! It's about to collapse!\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Haha! Brothers, sisters, do not be afraid!\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"'Tis merely my hammer summoning up a gale. See? A whoop, and a whoosh!\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Thus did he swing on, chiseling into the great mountain, sparks flying from the hammer's handle,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And they all looked on in joy and fear, as the champion's laurels he claimed!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "When Lady Mbande returned to the Lord of the Night's embrace,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sundjatta was already a young man, robust beyond his years."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "On the night when a chief was to be elected, he left the tribe alone,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Tribal champion though he was, Sundjatta aspired not to power,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But instead sought to find a proud testament to his existence as one of us,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Resolute was he, striking out on an adventure toward lands distant and foreign,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yet his passion was misunderstood by his tribespeople, who regarded him as a runaway, a traitor..."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-27cd7879327b631b"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "volumeKey": "vol-3",
      "label": "Vol. 3",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sundjatta, who had lost his good name by voluntarily embarking on an adventurous journey,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Headed to the distant lava lake, letting the scorching waves burn his body."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "This burning lake has now cooled, and dragons play havoc there no more,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But in those days, it was the abode ruled by the evil dragon Lukwata,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "One of the few survivors of the ancient dragon race,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Who, with malice in its heart, sought ever to restore ancient draconic tyranny."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The ancient war, which had rocked both heaven and earth, had destroyed its tribe,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But it hid in a dark, rocky cave, thus evading utter devastation."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Without servants to wait upon it, Lukwata had grown decrepit,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Eyes scorched blind by sulfur's breath, mind becoming dull and frenzied."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Inextricably trapped in a delirious dream of battle against heavenly envoys, clinging to life,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Unaware of the human epoch that had come upon Natlan."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "So when a tiny slave came to its hideout and issued a challenge,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The ancient dragon arose in fury, coughing and retching, hurling curses unceasingly,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Along with which spewed flames and sulfur from its maw,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"You insolent wretch! You dare disturb my royal slumber!?\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sundjatta saw that the vile dragon of legend had long become doddering and deranged,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "That it would claim a Sovereign's title while forgetting its race."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "So he burst into laughter, hoisting his massive hammer, and mocked the enfeebled drake:"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"I am merely a nameless miner, not some contemptible knave.\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Just as you are no king — merely a tottering lizard!\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Rage surged in Lukwata's throat upon hearing these words, and with more wild retching,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It spat forth filthy, scorching lava, billowing forth plumes of pitch-black smoke,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "At which Sundjatta did not even frown, instead swinging his heavy hammer down on the old drake."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Old and infirm was Lukwata, yet when enraged it remained terrifyingly formidable,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And as the great heat of the magma scorched Sundjatta's hair and eyebrows,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The dragon's fierce venom again seeped into flesh and viscera, the unbearable agony burning deep,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And its massive yellowed fangs left festering wounds, while sharpened claws tore open old scars."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yet on and on Sundjatta swung, enduring tremendous pain,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Until the dragon's craggy head split open, until the hammer-storm blew the black smog away."
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And when the elder dragon's soul had been scattered to the winds, and the magma lake had cooled by half,"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sundjatta lay down, contented — truly now did he deserve a hero's name!"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-4dd2ffe62ca3e159"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
